other primary glioblastoma (<bold>B</bold>). Moderate expression level (&#x0002b;&#x0002b;) of cytoplasmic Survivin was detected in a pre-existing low-graded (grade II) glioma (<bold>C</bold>), which was obviously lower than that in its paired secondary glioblastoma with a staining score of &#x0002b;&#x0002b;&#x0002b;&#x0002b; (<bold>D</bold>). High-level (&#x0002b;&#x0002b;&#x0002b;&#x0002b;) expression of nuclear Survivin was detected in a secondary glioblastoma (<bold>E</bold>) and its matched pre-existing grade II glioma (<bold>F</bold>). Three apoptotic cells with clear nuclear staining (green color) were examined in a primary glioblastoma (<bold>G</bold>).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="94-6602904f1"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Status of Survivin expression and apoptotic index in primary GBMs</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="left"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Case no.</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Age&#x0002f;sex</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Tumour size (cm)</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Cytoplasmic Survivin<sup>a</sup></bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Nuclear Survivin<sup>a</sup></bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>AI<sup>b</sup></bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">1</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">11&#x0002f;M</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">5.7</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x0002b;&#x0002b;&#x0002b;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charo